; expect 42
; `Mod::name` is the escape from the flat namespace that `AX3014`'s own
; help text tells the reader to write - "qualify the reference:
; `DupA::dup` or `DupB::dup`". Writing it still reported `AX3014`,
; because `checkAmbiguous` asked `bareOf name` and `bareOf` strips
; exactly the qualifier that answers the question. So the diagnostic
; recommended a spelling it then refused, and the documented way out of
; a name collision did not exist.
;
; Both halves are asserted. The first is that neither call is refused;
; the second, which is the one that matters, is that each resolves to
; the module it NAMES - a fix that only silenced the diagnostic could
; still bind both calls to whichever definition came first, and the
; answers here are 100 apart so that shows up as a value.
(import DupA)

(import DupB)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (if (&&
    (==
      (DupA::dup
        0
      )      1
    )    (==
      (DupB::dup
        0
      )      100
    )
  )
    42
    1
  )
)
